### Prevent duplicate shortcut execution (6/6)

**Severity:** `high`

Only the open flyout should handle context-menu shortcuts, and no receiver should process a message after it has already been handled. This prevents the primary shortcut from executing once through the command bar and again through the context menu. Apply all suggestions in this group together.

```suggestion
        if (msg.Handled || !IsFlyoutOpen)
        {
            return;
        }

        var result = ViewModel?.CheckKeybinding(msg.Ctrl, msg.Alt, msg.Shift, msg.Win, msg.Key);
```

